  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "vfs_crossrename — server side rename files across filesystem boundaries",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Synopsis",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs objects = crossrename"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This VFS module is part of the [[p0]] suite.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "samba(7)",
            "href": "https://www.samba.org/samba/docs/current/man-html/samba.7.html"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] VFS module allows server side rename operations even if source and target are on different physical devices. A \"move\" in Explorer is usually a rename operation if it is inside of a single share or device. Usually such a rename operation returns NT_STATUS_NOT_SAME_DEVICE and the client has to move the file by manual copy and delete operations. If the rename by copy is done by the server this can be much more efficient. vfs_crossrename tries to do this server-side cross-device rename operation.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs_crossrename"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "There are however limitations that this module currently does not solve:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This module is not fully stackable. It can be combined with other modules, but should be the last module in the [[p0]] list. It directly access the files in the OS filesystem.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs objects"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "crossrename:sizelimit = BYTES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "server-side cross-device-renames are only done for files if the filesize is not larger than the defined size in MiB to prevent timeouts. The default sizelimit is 20 (MiB)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "EXAMPLES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "To add server-side cross-device renames inside of a share for all files sized up to 50MB:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "VERSION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This man page is part of version 4.25.0 of the Samba suite.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The original Samba software and related utilities were created by Andrew Tridgell. Samba is now developed by the Samba Team as an Open Source project similar to the way the Linux kernel is developed.",
      "protected": []
    }
  ],
